{"id":"mahabharata-3-040","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":40,"title":"चत्वारिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 40 · Arjuna fights the mountain hunter","summary":{"en":"Shiva comes as a Kirata hunter with Uma, and he and Arjuna shoot the same boar demon at once. They quarrel over it and fight; Arjuna's arrows and blows have no effect, his bow is swallowed, and in a wrestling match he is crushed senseless; recognising Shiva, he falls at his feet, and Shiva embraces him.","kn":"ಶಿವನು ಉಮೆಯೊಂದಿಗೆ ಕಿರಾತ ಬೇಟೆಗಾರನಾಗಿ ಬರುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅವನೂ ಅರ್ಜುನನೂ ಏಕಕಾಲದಲ್ಲಿ ವರಾಹರೂಪದ ದಾನವನಿಗೆ ಬಾಣ ಹೊಡೆಯುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಅದಕ್ಕಾಗಿ ಜಗಳವಾಡಿ ಹೋರಾಡುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಅರ್ಜುನನ ಬಾಣ ಏಟುಗಳು ನಿಷ್ಫಲ, ಬಿಲ್ಲು ನುಂಗಲ್ಪಡುತ್ತದೆ, ಮಲ್ಲಯುದ್ಧದಲ್ಲಿ ಮೂರ್ಛಿತನಾಗುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಶಿವನೆಂದು ಅರಿತು ಪಾದಕ್ಕೆರಗಿದಾಗ ಶಿವನು ಅಪ್ಪಿಕೊಳ್ಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"शिव उमा के साथ किरात शिकारी बनकर आते हैं, और वे तथा अर्जुन एक साथ वराह-रूपी दानव पर बाण चलाते हैं। उसके लिए झगड़कर दोनों लड़ते हैं; अर्जुन के बाण और प्रहार निष्फल होते हैं, उनका धनुष निगल लिया जाता है और मल्लयुद्ध में वे मूर्च्छित हो जाते हैं; शिव को पहचानकर वे चरणों में गिरते हैं, और शिव उन्हें गले लगाते हैं।","te":"శివుడు ఉమతో కిరాత వేటగానిగా వస్తాడు; ఆయన, అర్జునుడు ఒకేసారి వరాహరూప దానవునిపై బాణం వేస్తారు. దాని కోసం కలహించి పోరాడతారు; అర్జునుని బాణాలు, దెబ్బలు నిష్ఫలమవుతాయి, విల్లు మింగబడుతుంది, మల్లయుద్ధంలో మూర్ఛపోతాడు; శివుడని గుర్తించి పాదాలపై పడగా శివుడు కౌగిలించుకుంటాడు.","ta":"ஶிவன் உமையுடன் கிராத வேடனாக வர, அவரும் அர்ஜுனனும் ஒரே நேரத்தில் பன்றி வடிவ அசுரன் மீது அம்பெய்கிறார்கள். அதற்காகச் சண்டையிட்டுப் போரிட, அர்ஜுனனின் அம்புகளும் அடிகளும் பயனற்றுப் போகின்றன, அவன் வில் விழுங்கப்படுகிறது, மல்யுத்தத்தில் மயங்கி விழுகிறான்; ஶிவன் என்று உணர்ந்து பாதங்களில் விழ, ஶிவன் அவனைத் தழுவுகிறார்.","ml":"ഉമയോടൊപ്പം കിരാതവേടനായി ശിവൻ വരുന്നു; കാട്ടുപന്നിരൂപത്തിലുള്ള ഒരസുരനെ ഇരുവരും ഒരുമിച്ച് അമ്പെയ്യുന്നു. അതിന്റെ പേരിൽ തർക്കിച്ച് അവർ യുദ്ധം ചെയ്യുന്നു; അർജുനന്റെ അമ്പുകൾക്കും പ്രഹരങ്ങൾക്കും ഫലമില്ല, വില്ല് വിഴുങ്ങപ്പെടുന്നു, മല്ലയുദ്ധത്തിൽ അദ്ദേഹം ബോധരഹിതനാകുംവിധം ഞെരുങ്ങുന്നു. ശിവനെ തിരിച്ചറിഞ്ഞ് അർജുനൻ പാദങ്ങളിൽ വീഴുന്നു; ശിവൻ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ ആലിംഗനം ചെയ്യുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.40; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"कैरातपर्व","titleEn":"Kairata Parva (The mountain hunter)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"गतेषु तेषु सर्वेषु तपस्विषु महात्मसु ।\nपिनाकपाणिर्भगवान्सर्वपापहरो हरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When all those great-souled ascetics had gone, the blessed Hara, the remover of all sins, wielder of the Pinaka bow in his hand,"}},{"n":2,"text":"कैरातं वेषमास्थाय काञ्चनद्रुमसंनिभम् ।\nविभ्राजमानो वपुषा गिरिर्मेरुरिवापरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"took on the form of a mountain hunter, gleaming like a golden tree, his body shining like a second Mount Meru."}},{"n":3,"text":"श्रीमद्धनुरुपादाय शरांश्चाशीविषोपमान् ।\nनिष्पपात महार्चिष्मान्दहन्कक्षमिवानलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking a splendid bow and arrows like venomous snakes, he sprang forth, blazing greatly like a fire burning dry grass."}},{"n":4,"text":"देव्या सहोमया श्रीमान्समानव्रतवेषया ।\nनानावेषधरैर्हृष्टैर्भूतैरनुगतस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was accompanied by the goddess Uma, dressed and vowed like himself, and by cheerful spirits in many kinds of dress."}},{"n":5,"text":"किरातवेषप्रच्छन्नः स्त्रीभिश्चानु सहस्रशः ।\nअशोभत तदा राजन्स देवोऽतीव भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hidden in the hunter's guise and followed by thousands of women, that god, O king, shone exceedingly."}},{"n":6,"text":"क्षणेन तद्वनं सर्वं निःशब्दमभवत्तदा ।\nनादः प्रस्रवणानां च पक्षिणां चाप्युपारमत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In an instant that whole forest fell silent; the sound of springs and the birds' calls ceased."}},{"n":7,"text":"स संनिकर्षमागम्य पार्थस्याक्लिष्टकर्मणः ।\nमूकं नाम दितेः पुत्रं ददर्शाद्भुतदर्शनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Coming close to Partha, whose deeds are effortless, he saw a wondrous-looking being, Muka, a son of Diti,"}},{"n":8,"text":"वाराहं रूपमास्थाय तर्कयन्तमिवार्जुनम् ।\nहन्तुं परमदुष्टात्मा तमुवाचाथ फल्गुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"who had taken the form of a boar and seemed to be planning to kill Arjuna; that very evil creature he saw, and Phalguna spoke to it."}},{"n":9,"text":"गाण्डीवं धनुरादाय शरांश्चाशीविषोपमान् ।\nसज्यं धनुर्वरं कृत्वा ज्याघोषेण निनादयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking the Gandiva bow and arrows like venomous snakes, stringing the best of bows and making it resound with the twang of the string, Arjuna said:"}},{"n":10,"text":"यन्मां प्रार्थयसे हन्तुमनागसमिहागतम् ।\nतस्मात्त्वां पूर्वमेवाहं नेष्यामि यमसादनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Since you wish to kill me, who came here without offense, I will send you to Yama's abode first.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"तं दृष्ट्वा प्रहरिष्यन्तं फल्गुनं दृढधन्विनम् ।\nकिरातरूपी सहसा वारयामास शंकरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Phalguna of the firm bow about to shoot, the hunter, who was Shankara, suddenly stopped him."}},{"n":12,"text":"मयैष प्रार्थितः पूर्वं नीलमेघसमप्रभः ।\nअनादृत्यैव तद्वाक्यं प्रजहाराथ फल्गुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This one, dark as a blue cloud, was first aimed at by me.\" But Phalguna, without heeding those words, shot."}},{"n":13,"text":"किरातश्च समं तस्मिन्नेकलक्ष्ये महाद्युतिः ।\nप्रमुमोचाशनिप्रख्यं शरमग्निशिखोपमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The hunter of great splendor likewise loosed at that same target an arrow like a thunderbolt, like a tongue of flame."}},{"n":14,"text":"तौ मुक्तौ सायकौ ताभ्यां समं तत्र निपेततुः ।\nमूकस्य गात्रे विस्तीर्णे शैलसंहनने तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The two arrows, loosed together, struck together the vast body of Muka, built like a rock."}},{"n":15,"text":"यथाशनिविनिष्पेषो वज्रस्येव च पर्वते ।\nतथा तयोः संनिपातः शरयोरभवत्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a thunderbolt crashes on a mountain, so was the collision of the two arrows then."}},{"n":16,"text":"स विद्धो बहुभिर्बाणैर्दीप्तास्यैः पन्नगैरिव ।\nममार राक्षसं रूपं भूयः कृत्वा विभीषणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pierced by many arrows like blazing-mouthed serpents, he died, resuming his own dreadful rakshasa form."}},{"n":17,"text":"ददर्शाथ ततो जिष्णुः पुरुषं काञ्चनप्रभम् ।\nकिरातवेषप्रच्छन्नं स्त्रीसहायममित्रहा ।\nतमब्रवीत्प्रीतमनाः कौन्तेयः प्रहसन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Jishnu saw a man bright as gold, hidden in a hunter's guise and accompanied by women; the slayer of enemies, the son of Kunti, glad at heart, spoke to him, as if smiling."}},{"n":18,"text":"को भवानटते शून्ये वने स्त्रीगणसंवृतः ।\nन त्वमस्मिन्वने घोरे बिभेषि कनकप्रभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Who are you, wandering in this empty forest surrounded by a band of women? Golden-bright one, are you not afraid in this dreadful forest?\""}},{"n":19,"text":"किमर्थं च त्वया विद्धो मृगोऽयं मत्परिग्रहः ।\nमयाभिपन्नः पूर्वं हि राक्षसोऽयमिहागतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Why did you strike this animal, which was my catch? It was first attacked by me; this rakshasa had come here.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"कामात्परिभवाद्वापि न मे जीवन्विमोक्ष्यसे ।\nन ह्येष मृगयाधर्मो यस्त्वयाद्य कृतो मयि ।\nतेन त्वां भ्रंशयिष्यामि जीवितात्पर्वताश्रय ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Whether from desire or from contempt, you will not escape me alive. What you have done to me today is not the dharma of hunting; for it I will drive you from life, you who take shelter in the mountain.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"इत्युक्तः पाण्डवेयेन किरातः प्रहसन्निव ।\nउवाच श्लक्ष्णया वाचा पाण्डवं सव्यसाचिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Addressed so by the Pandava, the hunter, with a smile, spoke gently to Savyasachi, the Pandava."}},{"n":22,"text":"ममैवायं लक्ष्यभूतः पूर्वमेव परिग्रहः ।\nममैव च प्रहारेण जीविताद्व्यवरोपितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This was my target and my prey from the first, and it was struck down from life by my blow.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"दोषान्स्वान्नार्हसेऽन्यस्मै वक्तुं स्वबलदर्पितः ।\nअभिषक्तोऽस्मि मन्दात्मन्न मे जीवन्विमोक्ष्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Proud of your own strength, you should not lay your faults on another. I have been challenged, fool; you will not escape me alive.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"स्थिरो भवस्व मोक्ष्यामि सायकानशनीनिव ।\nघटस्व परया शक्त्या मुञ्च त्वमपि सायकान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Stand firm; I will loose arrows like thunderbolts. Strive with all your might, and you also shoot your arrows.\""}},{"n":25,"text":"ततस्तौ तत्र संरब्धौ गर्जमानौ मुहुर्मुहुः ।\nशरैराशीविषाकारैस्ततक्षाते परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the two, full of fury and roaring again and again, cut each other with arrows like venomous snakes."}},{"n":26,"text":"ततोऽर्जुनः शरवर्षं किराते समवासृजत् ।\nतत्प्रसन्नेन मनसा प्रतिजग्राह शंकरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Arjuna showered a rain of arrows on the hunter, and Shankara received it with a pleased mind."}},{"n":27,"text":"मुहूर्तं शरवर्षं तत्प्रतिगृह्य पिनाकधृक् ।\nअक्षतेन शरीरेण तस्थौ गिरिरिवाचलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking that rain of arrows for a moment, the bearer of the Pinaka stood, unwounded in body, like an unmoving mountain."}},{"n":28,"text":"स दृष्ट्वा बाणवर्षं तन्मोघीभूतं धनंजयः ।\nपरमं विस्मयं चक्रे साधु साध्विति चाब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that shower of arrows made useless, Dhananjaya was greatly amazed and said, \"Well done, well done!\""}},{"n":29,"text":"अहोऽयं सुकुमाराङ्गो हिमवच्छिखरालयः ।\nगाण्डीवमुक्तान्नाराचान्प्रतिगृह्णात्यविह्वलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Ah, this one of delicate limbs, dwelling on the Himalaya peak, takes the iron arrows loosed from Gandiva unshaken.\""}},{"n":30,"text":"कोऽयं देवो भवेत्साक्षाद्रुद्रो यक्षः सुरेश्वरः ।\nविद्यते हि गिरिश्रेष्ठे त्रिदशानां समागमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Who is this god? Could he be Rudra himself, a yaksha, or a lord of the gods? On this best of mountains the gods come together.\""}},{"n":31,"text":"न हि मद्बाणजालानामुत्सृष्टानां सहस्रशः ।\nशक्तोऽन्यः सहितुं वेगमृते देवं पिनाकिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"No one other than the god Pinakin could endure the force of my thousands of arrows when loosed.\""}},{"n":32,"text":"देवो वा यदि वा यक्षो रुद्रादन्यो व्यवस्थितः ।\nअहमेनं शरैस्तीक्ष्णैर्नयामि यमसादनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Be he a god or a yaksha standing here other than Rudra, I will send him to Yama's abode with my sharp arrows.\""}},{"n":33,"text":"ततो हृष्टमना जिष्णुर्नाराचान्मर्मभेदिनः ।\nव्यसृजच्छतधा राजन्मयूखानिव भास्करः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Jishnu, glad of mind, loosed iron arrows that pierce vital spots, a hundredfold, O king, like the sun's rays."}},{"n":34,"text":"तान्प्रसन्नेन मनसा भगवाँल्लोकभावनः ।\nशूलपाणिः प्रत्यगृह्णाच्छिलावर्षमिवाचलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The blessed one, maker of the worlds, the trident-bearer, received them with a calm mind, like a mountain receiving a shower of stones."}},{"n":35,"text":"क्षणेन क्षीणबाणोऽथ संवृत्तः फल्गुनस्तदा ।\nवित्रासं च जगामाथ तं दृष्ट्वा शरसंक्षयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In a moment Phalguna's arrows were exhausted, and he became afraid, seeing his arrows gone."}},{"n":36,"text":"चिन्तयामास जिष्णुस्तु भगवन्तं हुताशनम् ।\nपुरस्तादक्षयौ दत्तौ तूणौ येनास्य खाण्डवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Jishnu thought of the blessed Fire, who had earlier given him the two inexhaustible quivers at Khandava."}},{"n":37,"text":"किं नु मोक्ष्यामि धनुषा यन्मे बाणाः क्षयं गताः ।\nअयं च पुरुषः कोऽपि बाणान्ग्रसति सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"What shall I shoot with my bow now that my arrows are gone? And this man, whoever he is, swallows all my arrows.\""}},{"n":38,"text":"अहमेनं धनुष्कोट्या शूलाग्रेणेव कुञ्जरम् ।\nनयामि दण्डधारस्य यमस्य सदनं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I will drive him with the tip of my bow, as one drives an elephant with a spear point, to the house of Yama, who bears the rod.\""}},{"n":39,"text":"संप्रायुध्यद्धनुष्कोट्या कौन्तेयः परवीरहा ।\nतदप्यस्य धनुर्दिव्यं जग्रास गिरिगोचरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The son of Kunti, slayer of enemy heroes, fought with the tip of his bow; but that mountain-dweller swallowed even that divine bow."}},{"n":40,"text":"ततोऽर्जुनो ग्रस्तधनुः खड्गपाणिरतिष्ठत ।\nयुद्धस्यान्तमभीप्सन्वै वेगेनाभिजगाम तम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Arjuna, his bow swallowed, stood with a sword in hand, wishing to end the battle, and rushed at him with speed."}},{"n":41,"text":"तस्य मूर्ध्नि शितं खड्गमसक्तं पर्वतेष्वपि ।\nमुमोच भुजवीर्येण विक्रम्य कुरुनन्दनः ।\nतस्य मूर्धानमासाद्य पफालासिवरो हि सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Exerting himself with the strength of his arm, the delight of the Kurus brought down on his head a sharp sword that would not have been stopped even by mountains; but reaching his head, that best of swords shattered."}},{"n":42,"text":"ततो वृक्षैः शिलाभिश्च योधयामास फल्गुनः ।\nयथा वृक्षान्महाकायः प्रत्यगृह्णादथो शिलाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Phalguna fought with trees and rocks; but the huge-bodied one received the trees and the rocks."}},{"n":43,"text":"किरातरूपी भगवांस्ततः पार्थो महाबलः ।\nमुष्टिभिर्वज्रसंस्पर्शैर्धूममुत्पादयन्मुखे ।\nप्रजहार दुराधर्षे किरातसमरूपिणि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then mighty Partha struck the blessed one in hunter's form, hard to assail, with fists like thunderbolts in touch, making smoke rise from his own face."}},{"n":44,"text":"ततः शक्राशनिसमैर्मुष्टिभिर्भृशदारुणैः ।\nकिरातरूपी भगवानर्दयामास फल्गुनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the blessed one in hunter's form beat Phalguna with terrible fists like Indra's thunderbolt."}},{"n":45,"text":"ततश्चटचटाशब्दः सुघोरः समजायत ।\nपाण्डवस्य च मुष्टीनां किरातस्य च युध्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a most dreadful crackling sound arose from the fists of the Pandava and the hunter as they fought."}},{"n":46,"text":"सुमुहूर्तं महद्युद्धमासीत्तल्लोमहर्षणम् ।\nभुजप्रहारसंयुक्तं वृत्रवासवयोरिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"For a good while there was a great battle that made the hair stand on end, with blows of the arms, like that of Vritra and Vasava."}},{"n":47,"text":"जहाराथ ततो जिष्णुः किरातमुरसा बली ।\nपाण्डवं च विचेष्टन्तं किरातोऽप्यहनद्बलात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then strong Jishnu struck the hunter with his chest, and the hunter too struck the struggling Pandava with force."}},{"n":48,"text":"तयोर्भुजविनिष्पेषात्संघर्षेणोरसोस्तथा ।\nसमजायत गात्रेषु पावकोऽङ्गारधूमवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"From the grinding of their arms and the rubbing of their chests, a fire with embers and smoke arose on their bodies."}},{"n":49,"text":"तत एनं महादेवः पीड्य गात्रैः सुपीडितम् ।\nतेजसा व्याक्रमद्रोषाच्चेतस्तस्य विमोहयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Mahadeva, crushing him with his limbs, overpowered him with his fiery energy in anger, bewildering his mind."}},{"n":50,"text":"ततो निपीडितैर्गात्रैः पिण्डीकृत इवाबभौ ।\nफल्गुनो गात्रसंरुद्धो देवदेवेन भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, with his limbs crushed, Phalguna seemed rolled into a lump, held tight in the body of the god of gods, Bharata."}},{"n":51,"text":"निरुच्छ्वासोऽभवच्चैव संनिरुद्धो महात्मना ।\nततः पपात संमूढस्ततः प्रीतोऽभवद्भवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He lost breath, squeezed by the great-souled one, and fell down senseless; then Bhava was pleased."}},{"text":"भगवानुवाच","meaning":{"en":"The blessed one said:"}},{"n":52,"text":"भो भो फल्गुन तुष्टोऽस्मि कर्मणाप्रतिमेन ते ।\nशौर्येणानेन धृत्या च क्षत्रियो नास्ति ते समः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"O Phalguna, I am pleased with your matchless deed; there is no warrior equal to you in this courage and steadiness.\""}},{"n":53,"text":"समं तेजश्च वीर्यं च ममाद्य तव चानघ ।\nप्रीतस्तेऽहं महाबाहो पश्य मां पुरुषर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Your radiance and strength today are equal to mine, blameless one. I am pleased with you, mighty-armed bull among men; look at me.\""}},{"n":54,"text":"ददानि ते विशालाक्ष चक्षुः पूर्वऋषिर्भवान् ।\nविजेष्यसि रणे शत्रूनपि सर्वान्दिवौकसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I give you eyes, wide-eyed one; you were a sage of old. You will conquer your enemies in battle, even all the dwellers in heaven.\""}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":55,"text":"ततो देवं महादेवं गिरिशं शूलपाणिनम् ।\nददर्श फल्गुनस्तत्र सह देव्या महाद्युतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Phalguna saw there the god Mahadeva, lord of the mountain, wielder of the trident, of great splendor, with the goddess."}},{"n":56,"text":"स जानुभ्यां महीं गत्वा शिरसा प्रणिपत्य च ।\nप्रसादयामास हरं पार्थः परपुरंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Falling to his knees and bowing his head to the ground, Partha, conqueror of enemy cities, appeased Hara."}},{"text":"अर्जुन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna said:"}},{"n":57,"text":"कपर्दिन्सर्वभूतेश भगनेत्रनिपातन ।\nव्यतिक्रमं मे भगवन्क्षन्तुमर्हसि शंकर ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Kapardin, lord of all beings, destroyer of Bhaga's eyes, forgive me my trespass, blessed Shankara.\""}},{"n":58,"text":"भवगद्दर्शनाकाङ्क्षी प्राप्तोऽस्मीमं महागिरिम् ।\nदयितं तव देवेश तापसालयमुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I came to this great mountain wishing to see you, lord, this best abode of ascetics that is dear to you, lord of gods.\""}},{"n":59,"text":"प्रसादये त्वां भगवन्सर्वभूतनमस्कृत ।\nन मे स्यादपराधोऽयं महादेवातिसाहसात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I seek to please you, blessed one, whom all beings revere; may this not be an offense on my part, Mahadeva, from too much rashness.\""}},{"n":60,"text":"कृतो मया यदज्ञानाद्विमर्दोऽयं त्वया सह ।\nशरणं संप्रपन्नाय तत्क्षमस्वाद्य शंकर ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This fight with you was done by me out of ignorance; forgive that today, Shankara, for I have come to you for refuge.\""}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":61,"text":"तमुवाच महातेजाः प्रहस्य वृषभध्वजः ।\nप्रगृह्य रुचिरं बाहुं क्षान्तमित्येव फल्गुनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The one of great radiance, with the bull on his banner, laughed and, taking Phalguna's splendid arm, said to him, \"It is forgiven.\""}}]}]}